The upcoming Hulu -Onyx Collective limited series &#8220; Victoria &#8221; has added four new cast members, Variety has learned.

Kyle MacLachlan (&#8220;Twin Peaks,&#8221; &#8220;Fallout&#8221;), Michael Hyatt (&#8220;The Wire,&#8221; &#8220;The Pitt&#8221;), Marwan Kenzari (&#8220;Aladdin,&#8221; &#8220;The Old Guard&#8221;), and J. Alphonse Nicholson (&#8220;Lanterns,&#8221; &#8220;P-Valley&#8221;) are all set to appear in the series, which was ordered at Hulu in September.

Previously announced cast members include Li Jun Li, Diane Lane, and Mark Duplass. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'Nobody Wants This' Season 3 Opens With 6.2 Million Views in Four Days Netflix Grapples With Digital-Ad Squeeze Amid Widening Glut of Streaming Commercials

The logline for the series states, &#8220;Set in the cutthroat world of San Francisco's elite, &#8216;Victoria' is an erotic thriller about a brilliant con artist (Li) who finds herself in a dark web of power, luxury and the crosshairs of a seductive killer who knows her secrets.&#8221;

MacLachlan will play Howard Shannon, who is described as &#8220;a razor-sharp businessman and co-founder of one of Silicon Valley's most prestigious VC firms. His relentless drive for success has no limits.&#8221; Hyatt will play Detective Thompson, said to be &#8220;one of SFPD's most-experienced detectives. She is a dogged investigator who leads with instinct.&#8221;

Kenzari will play Glen Martin, &#8220;an ambitious venture capitalist with deep connections to the San Francisco elite. He will do whatever it takes to carve out the status he feels he deserves.&#8221; And Nicholson will play Jack, &#8220;a reckless loose cannon and Max's (Li) partner in crime. He is willing to go to unimaginable lengths to pull off a grift.&#8221;

MacLachlan is repped by UTA, Entertainment 360, and Jackoway Austen Tyerman. Hyatt is repped by Buchwald, Color Creative, and Frankfurt Kurnit Klein and Selz. Kenzari is repped by CAA and Anonymous Content. Nicholson is repped by AC Management, CESD and Jackoway Austen Tyerman. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Christy Hall is the creator, writer, executive producer, and showrunner on "Victoria." Geeta Vasant Patel will direct the pilot and executive produce. Lilly Burns, Elise Henderson, and Tony Hernandez of Counterpart Studios executive produce, with Li co-producing in addition to starring.

Ryan McCartan , fresh off his starring role as Jay Gatsby in Broadway's &#8220;The Great Gatsby,&#8221; will make his theatrical debut as the lead in the indie crime drama &#8220;Only Good Feelings.&#8221; SNR Films is giving the title a limited New York run in February 2027.

Other cast members include Elias Kacavas (&#8220;Pretty Little Liars: Original Sin&#8221;), Heather Burns (&#8220;Manchester by the Sea&#8221;), Ajay Naidu (&#8220;Office Space&#8221;), Amanda Steele and Ryan Whitney Newman (&#8220;See Dad Run&#8221;). Shervin Nassi directed and co-wrote the screenplay with Grant Schumacher. Michael Marlon serves as a producer. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'Beef' Creator Lee Sung Jin Sets Netflix Projects With Ali Wong, Gene Hong Under New Banner Lila Pictures 'The Mosquito Bowl' Review: Football Heroes Take to the Battlefield in Peter Berg's Emptily Macho WWII Epic

According to an official logline, &#8220;Only Good Feelings,&#8221; which was shot entirely in New York City, follows &#8220;Benny (McCartan), who is haunted by guilt after his fianc&#xE9;e dies in a car accident. As he spirals, he reconnects with Kam (Kacavas), a troubled childhood friend who pulls him into robbery, insurance fraud and extortion as part of a desperate plan to flee to Mexico. What begins as an escape becomes a collision course with everything Benny has been running from.&#8221;

On the festival circuit, &#8220;Only Good Feelings&#8221; won best narrative film at the Manhattan Film Festival and best directorial debut at the Chicago Indie Film Awards. Its 2026 selections include the San Francisco Jewish Film Festival, Dallas Movie Fest, the SoCal Film Awards and the San Diego Independent Cinema Awards.

McCartan's Broadway debut was in 2018 as Fiyero in &#8220;Wicked.&#8221; In 2020, he took over as Hans in &#8220;Frozen&#8221; on Broadway. His most recent on-screen credit was for the 2022 CW thriller series &#8220;The Winchesters.&#8221;

&#8220; The Fall and Rise of Reggie Dinkins &#8221; is bringing in four guest stars for Season 2's Thanksgiving episode .

Variety has learned exclusively that Leslie Uggams (&#8220;Roots,&#8221; &#8220;Deadpool&#8221; franchise, &#8220;Empire&#8221;), Kecia Lewis (Broadway's &#8220;Hell's Kitchen,&#8221; &#8220;The Blacklist&#8221;), Pastor Shirley Caesar, and Derek Gaines (&#8220;The King of Staten Island,&#8221; &#8220;The Last OG&#8221;) will all appear in the episode, which airs Nov. 23 at 8:30 pm ET/PT on NBC and streaming the next day on Peacock. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'Stranger Things' Prequel Spinoff 'Other Worlds' Ordered to Series at Netflix Maya Jama Strikes Deal With Netflix (EXCLUSIVE)

The series stars Tracy Morgan as Reggie Dinkins, with Erika Alexander, Daniel Radcliffe, Precious Way, Jalyn Hall, and Bobby Moynihan also starring.

The logline for the episode states, &#8220;It's Thanksgiving at the Dinkins house and Brina (Way) is eager to prove herself to Reggie's mother, Gigi.&#8221;

Uggams will play Gigi Dinkins, who is described as &#8220;Reggie's loving mother who now lives in Florida. She comes to visit for Thanksgiving and will take any opportunity to spoil her soon &#x2014; and her former daughter-in-law, Monica (Alexander).&#8221;

Lewis will play Ruby, said to be &#8220;one of the Dinkins aunties at the house for Thanksgiving. She takes charge of the kitchen and enjoys introducing Englishman Arthur Tobin (Radcliffe) to the joys of a properly seasoned Thanksgiving.&#8221;

Caesar will play herself, with the legendary pastor coming to the Dinkins home to give the blessing on Thanksgiving. Gaines will play Clarence, &#8220;one of Reggie's cousins who is at the house for Thanksgiving. He fancies himself a man of the world but always ends up causing trouble for the family.&#8221;

Uggams is repped by BRS/Gage Talent Agency. Lewis is repped by Paradigm and The Rosenzweig Group. Gaines is reppred by Gersh and Curate Management. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In &#8220;The Fall and Rise of Reggie Dinkins,&#8221; Reggie is a former pro football star who seeks to rehab his image with a documentary produced by documentarian Arthur Tobin, who is seeking redemption of his own.

Robert Carlock and Sam Means serve as co-showrunners, writers, and executive producers. Tina Fey, Morgan, Eric Gurian, and David Miner also executive produce. Universal Television is the studio.

&#8220;The Joker's Wild&#8221; is coming back again.

Howie Mandel will host a reboot of the classic game show, which will begin production in November for a launch in broadcast syndication on CBS Owned Stations in fall 2027.

The revival will combine the familiar gameplay of the original program, which debuted in 1972 and was rebooted a couple of times throughout the decades, with new twists and a high-stakes bonus round. Related Stories Hollywood's Next Big Deal: Will Netflix Make an M&A Play for NBCU? 'Heartland' Review: Jessica Chastain Rocks a Stetson and a Swagger for a Soapy Nashville Noir

Two contestants compete by taking spins on the High Roller slot machine and answering trivia questions across different categories. Jokers are, of course, wild, increasing the points up for grabs. After three fast-paced rounds, the contestant with the most points wins the game. That winner moves on to the new Joker's Jackpot bonus round, where they'll face tempting deals with the Devil. If they manage to avoid the Devil, they will win a jackpot between $10,000 and $50,000. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

"I love that we're bringing &#8216;The Joker's Wild' back," said Mandel in a statement. "It's such a fun, crazy show, and getting to be a part of that is a real honor. There's something great about taking a show people have loved for years and seeing what you can do with it today. I'm excited to get in there, have some laughs, and probably make a little bit of a mess along the way. That's usually when I'm having the most fun."

Mandel is no stranger to game shows, having hosted &#8220;Deal or No Deal&#8221; in the 2000s. He is also a longtime judge of &#8220;America's Got Talent&#8221; and is the new host of &#8220;The Price Is Right Tonight.&#8221;

&#8220;The Joker's Wild&#8221; was created by Jack Barry, who hosted the program until his death in 1984. After the series endured a variety of iterations, it was briefly rebooted in 2017 with host Snoop Dogg. That version ran for two years, meaning the series will have been off the air for eight years by the time the Mandel reboot launches. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;&#8216;The Joker's Wild' is one of the most recognizable brands in game show history, with a format that combines trivia, unpredictability and big-money stakes,&#8221; said Suzanne Prete, president of game shows at Sony Pictures Television. &#8220;Howie brings exactly the kind of wit, energy and spontaneity that this game demands. With him at the helm, we're excited to introduce &#8216;The Joker's Wild' to a new generation of viewers and continue evolving this iconic franchise for today's audiences without losing the qualities that made it a favorite in the first place.&#8221;

The series is produced by Sony Pictures Television and executive produced by Mashawn Nix. The series will tape on the Sony Pictures Studios lot in Culver City, Calif.

Twenty years after Morgan Spector arrived in New York hoping to make a living as an actor, he has finally reached the point where he's No. 1 on the call sheet. All it took was becoming a sex symbol at 46.

After years spent bouncing between theater and prestige television, Spector's turn as railroad baron George Russell on HBO's The Gilded Age has made him an object of internet lust &#x2014; &#8220;Train Daddy,&#8221; to a particularly enthusiastic segment of the show's fan base &#x2014; and given him the sort of platform he's still figuring out what to do with. And now comes an even bigger leap: Spector is taking over as Robert Langdon, the globe-trotting Harvard symbologist Tom Hanks played in three blockbuster movies, in Netflix's upcoming adaptation of Dan Brown's The Secret of Secrets . It's easily the biggest role of Spector's career. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories TV 'The Gilded Age' Is Serving Up Ambition and Shame in Season 4 Return Movies 'Moonfish' Review: Morgan Spector and Lucy Liu Voice a Spare but Evocative Animated Sci-Fi Suffused With Loneliness

Although Spector is quick to qualify the achievement. &#8220;But my wife is No. 2,&#8221; he says, referring to spouse and Secrets co-star Rebecca Hall. &#8220;So I don't get to eat all the green M&Ms on set, if you know what I mean.&#8221;

Spector is currently experiencing one of the more interesting midcareer moments in Hollywood. Until relatively recently, he seemed comfortably settled into being one of those reliably excellent performers whose face audiences might recognize even if his name didn't immediately come to mind.

His growing celebrity has presented another complication. &#8220;My era of becoming somebody with a platform has also been a time of dramatic political change, and I'm an outspoken person,&#8221; Spector says. &#8220;Sometimes I'd like to get off social media, but then I'm abandoning a space that I can use to say things that matter. But then, I have to do all the things that make people want to come to the platform, which means taking pretty pictures of yourself. There's only so much reposting of &#8216;Democracy Now' that your average Instagram viewer wants&#xA0; to see.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In the years before The Gilded Age , Spector was doing what actors have traditionally done when nobody was asking them for selfies: looking for work. After graduating from Reed College and the American Conservatory Theater in San Francisco, he moved to New York, where in 2010 a two-line walk-on in the Broadway production of A View From the Bridge turned into a starring role opposite Liev Schreiber and Scarlett Johansson.

&#8220;I was living off Nostrand Avenue in Brooklyn at the time, and I would commute in to work every day in a state of euphoria,&#8221; he says. &#8220;It just felt like New York City was wrapping its arms around me and giving me all I've ever dreamed of. But then I had to calibrate and think, &#8216;OK, well, what else is possible now?' &#8220;

For a while, the answer was more work rather than stardom. Roles on Homeland and miniseries The Plot Against America followed, and when Spector auditioned to play George Russell on The Gilded Age , he saw the Julian Fellowes drama as a chance to add another solid credit &#x2014; and, with any luck, a steady job &#x2014; to his r&#xE9;sum&#xE9;.

&#8220;They originally talked about five seasons as being a way to complete the arc,&#8221; Spector says. &#8220;But I saw that [HBO head of drama] Francesca Orsi say she'd love it to run for 10 years, so who knows?&#8221;

What he didn't foresee was the way audiences would respond to George. &#8220;Somebody wrote a piece about how George and Bertha's [Carrie Coon] marriage was the sexiest thing on television, and I remember thinking, &#8216;What?!' &#8221; he says with a laugh. &#8220;The show is relatively chaste, especially for HBO, and we weren't really lingering in eroticism. But it was the first sign that, OK, people are connecting to this in a way that wasn't obvious to us as we were making it.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Then came Robert Langdon. When Spector read for The Secret of Secrets with showrunner Carlton Cuse, he was reminded of his Gilded Age audition &#x2014; another opportunity he wasn't entirely sure made sense for him.

&#8220;I didn't think I was right for the part, and I guess as I'm getting older, I'm realizing that I don't know what's going to work for me or what I'm going to be good at,&#8221; Spector adds with a laugh.

He is now filming The Secret of Secrets in Prague. The acting part, at least, he knows how to handle. The rest of his newfound celebrity is proving more complicated.

&#8220;They don't teach you about this part in school,&#8221; he says. &#8220;It's like, how many thirst traps are enough and how many are too many? We're making our way through the wilderness.&#8221;

