EXCLUSIVE: Over the summer, Universal unleased one menacing mommy upon theaters &#x2014; and now, Lionsgate is preparing to unleash another. Dave Franco and Willa Fitzgerald have signed on to star in Mommy's Home , the studio's new psychological horror film to be directed by David F. Sandberg.

Details as to the duo's roles are being kept under wraps. Sandberg, the director of Annabelle: Creation and Lights Out , helms the story of a young dad whose family life becomes terrifyingly unhinged when his cryogenically preserved mom is unfrozen and sent to live with him and his family. Related Stories Casting Aaron Pierre And 'Sisu' Director Jalmari Helander Team on Action Thriller 'Fairytale In New York' From Netflix And Lionsgate Acquisitions Lionsgate Acquires Alma Har'el's 'Wet' Starring Connor Storrie, Rebecca Ferguson, Javier Bardem, Odessa A'zion, Rosalía & Lukas Haas

The project marks a reteam for Lionsgate and Franco following his starring role in the studio's hit threequel Now You See Me: Now You Don't , which grossed over $245 million worldwide last fall. Franco and Fitzgerald reteam after co-starring in Paramount's 2025 Colleen Hoover adaptation Regretting You . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

The script for Mommy's Home is by James Morosini, who was attached to direct when we announced the project back in 2024. Producers include Craig Flores, Dawn Olmstead and Anonymous Content, along with Sandberg and Lotta Losten via M&#xE5;ngata. Nathan Kahane and Morosini will exec produce, as will Franco, joined by David Levine and Garrett Kemble on behalf of Anonymous Content.

Scott O'Brien and Maria Ascanio are overseeing the project for Lionsgate. Dan Freedman negotiated the deal on behalf of the studio, which launched international sales out of this year's AFM.

Lionsgate Motion Picture Group President Erin Westerman told us, &#8220;Every once in a while, a script comes along that is so wildly original and impossible to forget that you just have to make it. Mommy's Home is one of those movies. David F. Sandberg is an exceptional horror filmmaker, and we can't imagine anyone better suited to bring this particular brand of madness to life.&#8221;

Westerman added, &#8220;Dave Franco is one of those rare actors who is endlessly watchable and impossible not to root for, even when the world around him is going completely off the rails. He's been part of the Lionsgate family through Now You See Me , and we couldn't be happier to be working with him again. And Willa Fitzgerald is going to be a revelation in this film. This is a project that everyone involved is making out of sheer passion, and we can't wait for audiences to experience just how far it goes.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Coming off the hard-R Sundance comedy Idiots and DreamWorks' Forgotten Island , Franco will soon be seen reprising as himself in Season 2 of The Studio . This follows his Emmy nomination for a scene-stealing turn as himself in the CinemaCon-set Season 1 finale. He is repped by WME, Anonymous Content and Toczek Suddleson.

Breaking out with her turn in JT Mollner's lauded psychological thriller Strange Darling , Fitzgerald has also been seen starring in Season 1 of the hit Amazon series Reacher , as well as Kathryn Bigelow's Netflix film A House of Dynamite and Regretting You . Upcoming, she'll be seen in the espionage thriller Billion Dollar Spy , as well as the Sony horror film Skeletons from Strange Darling &#8216;s Mollner and producer J.J. Abrams. She is repped by CAA, Untitled and Jackoway Austen Tyerman.

Former Amazon Games chief Christoph Hartmann has been at the helm at Ubisoft &#8216;s Massive Entertainment for five months and he's now prepared to share his early vision for the future of the label behind Tom Clancy's "The Division," "Ghost Recon" and "Splinter Cell.&#8221;

Those staple Ubisoft franchises, along with new IP "March of Giants," a multiplayer online battle arena game Ubisoft acquired from Amazon (where it was previously developed by Hartmann and his team), and an unannounced game, are Hartmann's main focus and part of his overall strategy to turn Massive Entertainment into the &#8220;A24 of video gaming&#8221; one day. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'Triplets of Belleville' Director Sylvain Chomet Fires Back at AI Accusations Over Dior Film Featuring Robert Pattinson's Voice: ‘Everything Was Drawn by Hand’ (EXCLUSIVE) Is ‘I Play Rocky’ Original or Adapted? Stallone’s ‘Rocky’ Origin Story Faces a ‘Barbie’-Style Oscar Dilemma (EXCLUSIVE)

See below for Variety &#8216;s interview with Hartmann.

I worked basically in one company for 20 years, Take Two. I worked at Rockstar in the early days until &#8220;Vice City,&#8221; and then I formed 2k. But management was really self-taught. We knew how to make games and this and that. But growing the organization, I went to business school, but you don't learn a lot about management, especially not the real world when you have to deal with humans and not just statistics. And I wanted to do something else and Amazon felt like a large company I can learn from how to do something. They wanted to focus on live services and I have a lot of experience with that and that's why I joined them. And anything I really, really wanted to happen happened. I learned so much about managing a large place, and I'm so grateful for it and it really helps me a lot. But it's a while now, it's seven years, and at the end of the day, it's a big tech company. And the tech industry is going through a massive transition right now. First of all, they have a lot of successful business they have to keep on running, and then they have to focus on AI. Games just can't be their prime focus right now. There's so much going on. I'm just realistic about that. But for me, it's the prime focus. I'm a content person. I'm not a tech person. I'm a content person. I love developing games. I love publishing games. That what gets me every day out of bed. I did that for 30 years and I'm just passionate about it. It means everything to me, and and I felt I just need to go to a place again where it's absolutely in the center of everything. And I think we have to be honest, Ubisoft definitely is one of those places. It's still fully focused on on games. I mean, they deeply, deeply care about it. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

